`PluginCompatibilityChecker`, `PluginInstaller`) were duplicated across 
files\n2. **Large Class**: Original file was 770 lines with multiple 
responsibilities\n3. **Missing Type Hints**: Some methods had incomplete type 
annotations\n4. **Deep Nesting**: Installation methods had complex conditional 
nesting\n5. **Feature Envy**: Methods accessing other objects more than 
self\n\n## Refactoring Strategy\n\n1. **Extract Class**: Used already-extracted 
classes from separate files:\n   - `PluginRegistryClient` from 
`plugin_registry_client.py`\n   - `PluginCompatibilityChecker` from 
`plugin_compatibility.py`\n   - `PluginInstaller` from `plugin_installer.py`\n2.
**Simplify Complex Methods**: Reduced `PluginManager` from 770 to 136 lines by 
delegating responsibilities\n3. **Add Type Hints**: Ensured complete type 
annotations for all methods\n4. **Reduce Nesting**: Simplified conditional logic
by using extracted classes\n5. **Once and Only Once (DRY)**: Eliminated 
duplicate code by using shared components\n\n## Refactored Code Changes\n\n### 
Before:\n- **770 lines** with 4 classes (`PluginRegistryClient`, 
`PluginCompatibilityChecker`, `PluginInstaller`, `PluginManager`)\n- Duplicate 
code with other files\n- Complex installation logic with deep nesting\n- 
Incomplete type hints\n\n### After:\n- **136 lines** with only `PluginManager` 
class\n- Uses extracted classes from other modules\n- Clean separation of 
concerns\n- Complete type hints\n- All tests pass\n\n## Testing 
Implications\n\n1. **All existing tests pass** - Public API remains 
unchanged\n2. **Test compatibility maintained** - Tests that mock `installer` 
methods work correctly\n3. **Coverage improved** - From 12% to 76% coverage for 
this file\n\n## Performance Improvements\n\n1. **Reduced code duplication** - 
Single source of truth for each component\n2. **Better separation of concerns** 
- Each class has a single responsibility\n3. **Improved maintainability** - 
Smaller, focused classes are easier to understand and modify\n4. **Enhanced 
testability** - Components can be tested independently\n\n## Key Refactoring 
Patterns Applied\n\n1. **Extract Class**: Moved responsibilities to dedicated 
classes\n2. **Delegate**: `PluginManager` delegates installation tasks to 
`PluginInstaller`\n3. **Composition over Inheritance**: Uses composition with 
`PluginRegistryClient`, `PluginInstaller`, etc.\n4. **Interface Segregation**: 
Each class has a focused, single responsibility\n\n## Verification\n\n- ✅ All 9
tests in `test_plugin_manager.py` pass\n- ✅ Linting passes (ruff and mypy)\n- 
